# Trivy vulnerability ignore list
# Format: CVE-ID or ignore rule
# See: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/vulnerability/scanning/ignore/

# Alpine base image vulnerabilities - not exploitable in containerized contexts
# where the vulnerable packages are not actively used or exposed.
# Our containers run as non-root users with minimal attack surface.

# Ignore vulnerabilities in packages not used at runtime:
# - busybox: Not used in runtime (we only run Java/Node)
# - musl libc: Low impact in containerized environments
# - apk: Package manager not exposed to external access

# Add specific CVEs here after reviewing scan results
# To ignore all unfixed vulnerabilities, use:
# "*"

# To ignore specific severity for specific packages:
# "CVE-2024-XXXX"  # reason for ignoring
